    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1552">

                <pb facs="1158" n="1042" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1042"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/629.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Garrett to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Nuevo Laredo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 2, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>By order of General Luis Caballero, military governor of Tamaulipas, 19,300
                    pesos, Villista currency, was taken from José Pereda, a <pb facs="1159" n="1043"
                        xml:id="pg1043"/> Spanish merchant of Monterey, by military authorities here
                    to-day. Department can take such action as they deem appropriate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
